<title>USA: The top cold remedies, and their makers.</title>
<headline>The top cold remedies, and their makers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>What is the pecking order in cough-cold-allergy brands?</p>
<p>According to Information Resources, this is the most recent market-share breakdown:</p>
<p>Tylenol (McNeil Consumer Products), 9.8 percent</p>
<p>Robitussin (Whitehall-Robins), 9.1 percent</p>
<p>Benadryl (Warner-Lambert), 6.4 percent</p>
<p>Sudafed (Warner-Lambert), 6.1 percent</p>
<p>NyQuil (Procter &amp; Gamble), 5.4 percent</p>
<p>Alka-Seltzer (Bayer), 4.7 percent</p>
<p>Dimetapp (Whitehall-Robins), 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>The corporate sales totem-pole finds Procter &amp; Gamble at the top with a 13 percent market share; Warner-Lambert next with 11 percent and Bayer third with 8 percent.</p>
</text>
